case file to continue to deliver quality content. With Greg Dumasevich's second police interview failing to generate any new leads or answers, the search for Jaden Leski continued. Local waterways, including Lake Narakan and the swamp in Edward Hunter Reserve were drained. while 140 police and SES volunteers searched 54 hectares of surrounding bushland. On June 25, 10 days into Jaden's disappearance, search parties began combing the local rubbish tip, wearing masks to shield themselves from the rancid odors that permeated around them. Police helicopters equipped with thermal imaging equipment circled overhead

